  <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
  <h1>Targets</h1>
  <p class="lede">A target tells a category how much to assign each month.</p>

  <section class="guide-split">
    <div class="copy">
  <h2>Monthly</h2>
  <p>Monthly is a fixed amount to assign every month. Money left at the end of the month stays in the category, ready to spend. Next month assigns the same amount.</p>

  <h2>Fill up to</h2>
  <p>Keep the category topped up to the target each month. Money left over counts toward the next month, so that month asks for less. If more than the target is still there, Auto-Assign can return the extra to Ready to Assign.</p>

  <h2>Save by date</h2>
  <p>Reach the target by a future month. ZxBudget splits what is still needed across the months up to that date. The date is a month, not a day.</p>

    </div>
